    {
      "unit_id": "qrm-control-chart-l9-note-f6d674a13145:p0008:text",
      "course_id": "qrm",
      "document_id": "qrm-control-chart-l9-note-f6d674a13145",
      "kind": "page_text",
      "text": "Exercise 2\n\nA control chart is to be constructed for the average breaking strength of\nnylon fibers. Samples of size 5 are randomly chosen from the process.\nThe process mean and standard deviation are estimated to be 120 kg\nand 8 kg, respectively.\n\na)   If the control limits are placed three standard deviations from the\n   process mean, what is the probability of a type I error?\n\nb)  If the process mean shifts to 125 kg, what is the probability of\n   concluding that the process is in control and hence making a type II\n    error on the first sample plotted after the shift?\n\nc) What is the probability of detecting the shift by the second sample\n    plotted after the shift if the samples are chosen independently?\n\n\n\n\n\n                ME3327E QUALITY, RELIABILITY AND MAINTENANCE",
      "locator": {
        "page": 8,
        "slide": 8,
        "bbox": null
      },
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "Quality_Reliability_Maintenance_Control_Chart_Note_L9.pdf",
        "source_sha256": "f6d674a13145ca2f13d03f9245c235858af6380ace52dfdc53d6acf480485ae7",
        "extractor": "pymupdf",
        "extracted_at": "2026-09-03T07:07:41.890331+00:00",
        "model": null,
        "parent_unit_id": null
      },
      "review_status": "approved",
      "content_hash": "628e44eeca7645fbecaf3597019d42ca1278ff70e4e4abfa8af3feb356149da5",
      "metadata": {
        "layout_blocks": [
          {
            "bbox": [
              7.2,
              6.19,
              141.38,
              39.19
            ],
            "text": "Exercise 2",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              7.2,
              60.34,
              708.6,
              170.76
            ],
            "text": "A control chart is to be constructed for the average breaking strength of \nnylon fibers. Samples of size 5 are randomly chosen from the process. \nThe process mean and standard deviation are estimated to be 120 kg \nand 8 kg, respectively.",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              7.2,
              185.64,
              684.82,
              209.64
            ],
            "text": "a) If the control limits are placed three standard deviations from the",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              43.2,
              214.46,
              575.64,
              238.46
            ],
            "text": "process mean, what is the probability of a type I error?",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              7.2,
              253.22,
              647.66,
              277.22
            ],
            "text": "b) If the process mean shifts to 125 kg, what is the probability of",
            "block_type": 0
          },
          {
            "bbox": [
              43.2,
              282.02,
              701.26,
              334.82
            ],
            "text": "concluding that the process is in control and hence making a type II \nerror on the first sample plotted after the shift?",
